From abebd61d0032deb198cfb2c829c13720047e667f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:05:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: add the MT6370 Type-C port in sink-only
 mode

With the charger node in place the MT6370 runs its own BC1.2 engine, but
nothing tells the port controller what is on the other end of the cable,
and the stock DT has a full tcpc-dual/type_c_port0 stack for it (live DT:
mt6370_pd_eint on GPIO41, mt-tcpc role_def 0x04). Add the mainline
equivalent, deliberately reduced.

The connector child is not optional: tcpci_parse_config() looks up a child
named "connector" and fails the probe with "Can't find connector node."
otherwise (drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci.c: tcpci_parse_config), and tcpm
re-reads the same fwnode in tcpm_register_port(). Of the connector
properties power-role is the only mandatory one (typec_get_fw_cap(),
drivers/usb/typec/class.c:2233); sink-pdos is mandatory as soon as the
port is a sink (tcpm.c:7315), source-pdos is not even read for
TYPEC_PORT_SNK (tcpm.c:7287).

Sink-only on purpose. The tablet's only interactive channel is the RNDIS
gadget, and letting tcpm drive the USB role is what killed it before:

  - tcpm resolves the role switch from the connector fwnode through the
    endpoint graph (fwnode_usb_role_switch_get, drivers/usb/roles/class.c:
    190 -> fwnode_graph_devcon_matches, drivers/base/property.c:1293) and
    then requires class device whose fwnode is the remote port parent,
    i.e. &ssusb, with the property "usb-role-switch" present;
  - mtu3 only reads that property and registers the switch when
    dr_mode != "peripheral" (mtu3_plat.c:275 early-out before line 302),
    so with our dr_mode the lookup returns -EPROBE_DEFER and the TCPC
    would never probe;
  - if the port were moved to dr_mode = "otg" instead, mtu3's default
    role is HOST unless role-switch-default-mode = "peripheral"
    (mtu3_dr.c:287-291), i.e. the port would come up as a host.

So neither ports/endpoint graph nor usb-role-switch is added: tcpm gets no
role switch, keeps its hands off the PHY/MAC, and &u2port0's
mediatek,force-device-mode plus dr_mode = "peripheral" stay authoritative.
Charging does not depend on the TCPC at all - the charger node is a
separate MFD child - so this patch is safe to drop if the TCPC misbehaves.

Also not added: usb-otg-vbus-regulator. tcpci_mt6370 looks for a "vbus"
supply on the tcpc node, not on the connector (devm_regulator_get_optional
(dev, "vbus"), tcpci_mt6370.c: mt6370_tcpc_probe), and when it is absent
tcpci_set_vbus() still exists and falls back to the standard TCPCI
SRC/SINK VBUS commands (tcpci.c:523), so tcpm_register_port() does not
fail. The boost is only needed to source VBUS, which a sink-only port
never does.

Requires CONFIG_TYPEC=y, CONFIG_TYPEC_TCPM=y, CONFIG_TYPEC_TCPCI=y,
CONFIG_TYPEC_TCPCI_MT6370=y (all currently =m, and the image ships no
modules).

To verify on hardware: /sys/class/typec/port0 exists with power_role
sink, dmesg shows no "Can't find connector node." / "Failed to register
tcpci port", RNDIS still enumerates on the host, and /sys/class/
power_supply/mt6370-charger/usb_type follows the attached charger.
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts  | 57 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
index 860f6fa8c..b3479760c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/iio/adc/mediatek,mt6370_adc.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/usb/pd.h>
 
 #include "mt6771.dtsi"
 #include "mt6358.dtsi"
@@ -310,6 +311,62 @@ charger {
 				      <&mt6370_adc MT6370_CHAN_IBAT>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Type-C port controller, sink only.
+		 *
+		 * The alert pad is GPIO41 (stock DT: mt6370_pd_eint,
+		 * interrupts = <0x29 ...>; mt6771-next: <&pio 41>), and it is
+		 * a different pad from the PMIC interrupt on GPIO10 above.
+		 * interrupts-extended is mandatory here: the node's parent is
+		 * the MT6370 irqchip, so plain "interrupts" would be decoded
+		 * as an MT6370 hw number.
+		 *
+		 * The connector child is mandatory, tcpci_parse_config() fails
+		 * with "Can't find connector node." without a child named
+		 * exactly "connector" (drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci.c:
+		 * tcpci_parse_config), and tcpci_mt6370 then hands that
+		 * fwnode to tcpm_register_port(). power-role is mandatory
+		 * there (typec_get_fw_cap(), drivers/usb/typec/class.c:2233);
+		 * with power-role = "sink" tcpm never reads source-pdos and
+		 * never tries to source VBUS (tcpm.c:7287), while sink-pdos
+		 * is required for a sink port (tcpm.c:7315).
+		 *
+		 * Deliberately no ports/endpoint graph to &ssusb and no
+		 * usb-role-switch on &ssusb: tcpm finds a role switch through
+		 * the connector's graph endpoints (fwnode_connection_find_
+		 * match -> fwnode_graph_devcon_matches, drivers/base/
+		 * property.c:1293) and would then drive mtu3's role. mtu3
+		 * only registers that switch when its node has
+		 * "usb-role-switch" and dr_mode != peripheral
+		 * (mtu3_plat.c:275/302), and its default role is host unless
+		 * role-switch-default-mode says otherwise (mtu3_dr.c:287).
+		 * So the graph link would either flip our RNDIS port to host
+		 * or - in peripheral mode - make tcpm defer forever on a role
+		 * switch nobody registers. Neither is needed to charge: the
+		 * charger above is an independent BC1.2 engine.
+		 *
+		 * pd-disable keeps the PD state machine out of the picture
+		 * for the first bring-up; sink-pdos documents the single 5 V
+		 * contract the port accepts.
+		 */
+		tcpc {
+			compatible = "mediatek,mt6370-tcpc";
+			interrupts-extended = <&pio 41 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+			connector {
+				compatible = "usb-c-connector";
+				label = "USB-C";
+
+				power-role = "sink";
+				data-role = "device";
+				pd-disable;
+				op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
+
+				sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000,
+						       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		regulators {
 			dsvbst {
 				regulator-name = "mt6370-dsv-vbst";
-- 
2.53.0

